---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { strings } from '../../i18n/strings';
import { getAllNames, getMeaningCoverageCount } from '../../lib/names';
const t = strings.en;
const nameCount = getAllNames().length;
const meaningCount = getMeaningCoverageCount();
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title={`About | ${t.brand}`} description="The NévnapTárX mission: preserving the Hungarian nameday tradition with modern technology." altLangPath="/about">
  <article class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl pt-3 lg:pt-10">
    <nav class="nx-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol><li><a href="/en/">{t.brand}</a></li><li aria-hidden="true">›</li><li aria-current="page">About</li></ol>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="mt-6 nx-page-title nx-page-title--sm nx-rise">About</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-nx-muted">Preserving the Hungarian nameday tradition with modern technology.</p>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-nx-muted leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">Mission</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Nameday is a beautiful, centuries-old Hungarian tradition — every day of the year is associated with one or more names that families and friends celebrate. In the digital age it's easy to forget.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">NévnapTárX was built with one simple goal: prevent that. The current calendar indexes namedays for <strong>{nameCount} distinct name forms</strong> and includes short meaning entries for <strong>{meaningCount} names</strong>. The iOS and Android apps can also provide daily reminders.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">What we offer</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li>Namedays for <strong>{nameCount} distinct name forms</strong></li>
          <li><strong>{meaningCount} short name meanings</strong>, with missing entries clearly labelled</li>
          <li>Every recurring calendar date, including 29 February</li>
          <li><strong>Daily push notifications</strong> for important namedays</li>
          <li><strong>Modern UI/UX</strong> with dark and light themes</li>
          <li><strong>Greeting suggestions</strong> for several situations</li>
          <li><strong>Completely free</strong>, ad-free base tier</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">The developer</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">NévnapTárX is built by <strong>Renátó Bogár</strong>, a Hungarian developer — out of love for Hungarian tradition. The project welcomes feedback and ideas.</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><a href="mailto:bogarrenato@gmail.com" class="text-nx-accent underline">bogarrenato@gmail.com</a></p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">Support</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">This is a solo side project with no company backing. If you find the work valuable and want it to continue:</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><a href="https://ko-fi.com/bogarrenato" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 h-12 px-6 rounded-full bg-[#ffb95c] hover:bg-[#ffc87f] text-[#1a1206] font-bold transition-[transform,background-color] duration-300 hover:-translate-y-0.5"><svg class="size-[1.125rem]" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 9h13v5a5 5 0 0 1-5 5H9a5 5 0 0 1-5-5V9z"/><path d="M17 10h1.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 0 5H17"/><path d="M8 3v2.5M12 3v2.5"/></svg> Buy me a coffee</a></p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nx-ink">Sources</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Nameday dates are traditional rather than official records, and calendars can differ. The Hungarian <a href="/adatbazis" class="text-nx-accent underline">database and methodology page</a> documents scope, limitations, review and primary references.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
